Subject: [PATCH] panvk: write_image_view_desc deals with images, not samplers

This function deals with images, which needs to patch texture-views, not
samplers. This is likely just copy-paste from write_sampler_desc().

Hopefully helps with flakiness in this VK CTS test case:
- dEQP-VK.robustness.robustness2.push.notemplate.rg32ui.unroll.nonvolatile.sampled_image.no_fmt_qual.null_descriptor.samples_1.3d.frag

Fixes: a789867cb452 ("panvk/v10+: Implement nullDescriptor support")
Reviewed-by: Lars-Ivar Hesselberg Simonsen <lars-ivar.simonsen@arm.com>
Reviewed-by: Boris Brezillon <boris.brezillon@collabora.com>
(cherry picked from commit 0ac3efa9f4f99ece07971de98360f339a1dc8803)

Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45704>
(cherry picked from commit fa51e0e4ece)

Backported to the 26.2.4-based fork: the src/ hunks applied as is; .pick_status.json (not in the fork's
history as such) was left out.

Generated-by: LLM
